From 5b0dac511b000c009bbe9ecd0357a61700d88cab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vlad777442 <vefirst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:51:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] bluestore: metadata-only move of an unshared object into
 the meta collection

OP_COLL_MOVE_RENAME with cid != dest_cid is now accepted when the
destination is the meta collection and the object references no shared
blob (ReplicaVault zero-copy vault). No on-disk format change:

- onode and extent-shard keys are rewritten under the new oid (as _rename);
- omap keys, which embed the collection's pool, are rewritten under the
  meta pool (O(keys), as _clone's omap copy);
- the onode and its blobs are re-homed into the meta collection's
  OnodeSpace and caches (the per-onode part of Collection::split_cache),
  leaving a non-existent placeholder at the old oid;
- the object's statfs contribution (computed as fsck does) moves from the
  source pool to the meta pool through a second per-pool delta on the
  TransContext, written to the existing PREFIX_STAT keys.

No block is allocated or released. Shared-blob objects are refused: the new
ObjectStore::can_move_to_collection() lets callers check first and copy
instead; a move issued anyway returns -EXDEV, which the transaction treats
as a no-op. Store-wide perf counters see the net (zero) delta.

Tests: ObjectStore/RVMoveTest (bluestore) - small/large objects, sharded
extent map with spanning blobs, 20k omap keys and xattrs, forced
compression, move queued after an uncommitted write, 50 moves then removing
the source collection, shared blob refused. Each checks the source is
ENOENT, data/xattrs/omap in meta, remount, deep fsck, per-pool statfs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GapZ5dvT4vTJ9FHbVNTeKb
